  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with Omar Jensen as lead developer for the development phase. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research and expanded its team with Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the prototype for secure file sharing, which was tested ahead of schedule. The executive board approved a $2M budget covering all phases. The next phase involves user interface enhancements starting in October, with feedback on the prototype sought by the end of November. Celebrations for the testing milestone are scheduled for October 10th."
